# Nougat OCR stub

**Status:** not-run (paper acquired via arXiv PDF; text extracted via `pdftotext`).

**Reason:** The paper (arXiv:2010.14821v2 — Zeng et al., "Simulating noisy variational quantum
eigensolver with local noise models") is a native LaTeX-generated arXiv preprint. Its selectable
text was fully recovered by `pdftotext`, obviating the need for OCR. All quoted claim numbers,
Table I values, Fig. 3 curve descriptions, and Eq. (6) noise-model definition used in this
replication were sourced from that pdftotext dump.

**Where the extracted text lives:**
- `../work/paper.pdf`  — original arXiv PDF
- `../work/paper.txt`  — pdftotext extraction (used as ground-truth for claim extraction and
  ansatz spec reconstruction; see `../report/REPORT.md` §3.c which mirrors the paper Fig. 2
  ansatz definition byte-for-byte from that text).

**If Nougat OCR were required later** (e.g., to recover equation-typeset math cleanly for a
downstream re-check of Eq. 6's Kraus operator form), the standard invocation would be:

```
nougat ../work/paper.pdf -o ../extraction/ --recompute
```

That command was NOT run in this replication because:
1. Free-endpoint budget was reserved for the actual VQE simulation.
2. Nougat's advantage is scanned/photographed pages; arXiv PDFs already carry a text layer.
3. Every numeric value used in this replication is quoted verbatim (with paper section reference)
   in `../report/REPORT.md` and could be re-verified by manual inspection of `../work/paper.pdf`.

**Provenance note:** this stub was created as part of the 2026-07-06 backfill packaging pass
(see `../report/workflow.md` §8). It documents the "extraction" artifact class for consistency
with the REPLICATE-PROJECT 8-artifact standard, even though no OCR step was actually needed.
